# cat — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R50
# Doc:  design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §4.5 and §5.5 in the paideia-os
#       repo. This file is the invariant-I6 (capability handoff visible
#       + refusable) manifest the shell validates at exec: cat receives
#       exactly the caps below and no more.
#
# The four caps below are the minimum surface for the reader to
# (1) identify who is reading (KIND_USER for the FileReadRecord audit
# tail at M3), (2) locate and read the file(s) named on argv
# (KIND_PDXFS_FILE narrowed to <arg-path> — one such cap per
# positional file argument, so a `cat a b c` invocation carries three
# read caps and can touch nothing else), (3) render bytes to the
# invoker's terminal (KIND_TTY narrowed to write, no read /
# tcsetattr), and (4) participate in the semantic-pipe layer
# (KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT for M3-001 schema-typed passthrough / M3-002
# RawByteChunk[] emission — declared here at M1 so consumers can
# inspect the manifest early; the wire binding lands at M3).
#
# Missing caps in the received set → exit 4 (cap denied per I4 in
# design/tooling/plan.md §4.2). Extra caps in the received set → the
# shell's exec-time cap_manifest_verify (libpdx-cap M2-001) refuses at
# the shell side; cat never sees them.
#
# Per-argument narrowing note
# ---------------------------
# The `KIND_PDXFS_FILE(read, <arg-path>)` line reads as "one cap per
# positional file argument". `cat a b c` receives three distinct
# KIND_PDXFS_FILE(read) caps — one for each of a, b, c. The shell
# constructs these from the invoker's cap environment at exec via
# libpdx-cap M2's cap_pack with `narrow_rights`; no wildcard subtree
# is ever granted. If argv has zero positionals, cat reads from stdin
# (KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT); no KIND_PDXFS_FILE cap is needed on that path.
requires:
  - KIND_USER
  - KIND_TTY(write)
  - KIND_PDXFS_FILE(read, <arg-path>)
  - KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT

# Declared output schemas — the semantic-pipe records cat emits.
# Declared at M1 (this file) so consumers can inspect the manifest;
# the actual wire binding + emission lands at M3-001 (schema-typed
# passthrough) and M3-002 (RawByteChunk for schemaless files) per
# r49-r50-plan.md §5.5.
declares_output_schemas:
  - RawByteChunk@0.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# R90-XREPO.013.M3-002 adoption note (cat#26, Wave L / v1.2.1-A)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# design/round-retrospectives/r90-xrepo-wave3-plan.md §"R90-XREPO.013.
# M3-002 cat -- caps.decl + adoption" ("Scope: As .013.M3-001, for cat.
# Same shape.") calls for exactly the four `requires:` kinds already
# declared above (KIND_USER, KIND_PDXFS_FILE, KIND_TTY, KIND_IPC_
# ENDPOINT) -- this file predates the M3-002 ticket (landed at R50 M1)
# but its cap set is byte-for-byte the shape M3-002 asks for, so no
# `requires:` edit was needed to reconcile; this note is the adoption
# record M3-002 itself is.
#
# The M3-002 scope's OTHER half -- "wire the libpdx-cap helper at
# entry; refuse to run if reconciliation narrows below required set"
# -- is NOT landed in src/entry.pdx and cannot land yet: M3-002 is
# gated on .013.M1-002 (the libpdx-cap client helper -- "Repo-side
# test drives the helper against a mock kernel"; not shipped in any
# repo at this writing) and .013.M2-001 (shell's real exec-time
# reconciliation wire-in). paideia-os/shell#39 documents shell's own
# side of M2-001 (CHANGELOG.md "exec-time reconciliation framing in
# sys_execve path") but shell's own src/exec.pdx still marks step (3)
# `cap_manifest_verify` as "DEFERRED (libpdx-cap not linked)" at shell
# HEAD -- the reconciled-set enforcement this manifest's own header
# comment describes ("the shell's exec-time cap_manifest_verify...
# refuses at the shell side") does not run yet anywhere in the stack.
# See STATUS.md's Wave L section for the external-gate tracking.
